==============================================================================
PART 3a -- MOD 9 FORBIDDEN-VALUES LAW (PROVED by finite exhaustion)
==============================================================================
cube residues mod 9 = [0, 1, 8]  (i.e. {0, +1, -1} mod 9)
attainable residues of x^3+y^3+z^3 mod 9 = [0, 1, 2, 3, 6, 7, 8]
FORBIDDEN residues mod 9 = [4, 5]  (i.e. +-4 mod 9)
  [PASS] forbidden set mod 9 == {4,5}: got [4, 5], expected [4, 5]
PROVED: x^3+y^3+z^3 is never == 4 or 5 (mod 9).  Proof: cube map factors
through Z/9 (in fact (x+3)^3 == x^3 mod 9), so the 9-case + 27-triple
exhaustion above is a complete case analysis, not a sampled pattern.

==============================================================================
PART 3b -- +-3 MOD 9 RIGIDITY LAW (why the stubborn k all look alike)
==============================================================================
  [PASS] sum == 3 (mod 9)  ==>  x == y == z == 1 (mod 3)   [729/729 triples]
  [PASS] sum == 6 (mod 9)  ==>  x == y == z == 2 (mod 3)   [729/729 triples]
PROVED: for k == +-3 (mod 9) every solution is 'rigid': all of x,y,z lie in
a single residue class mod 3.  This kills ~26/27 of the naive search space
and is the standard explanation of why the hard cases concentrate there.

==============================================================================
PART 3c -- MOD 7 GIVES NO OBSTRUCTION (PROVED)
==============================================================================
cube residues mod 7 = [0, 1, 6]  (i.e. {0, +1, -1} mod 7)
attainable residues of x^3+y^3+z^3 mod 7 = [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]
  [PASS] all 7 residues attained mod 7: got [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6], expected [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]
PROVED, with the clean reason: cube residues mod 7 are {0,+1,-1}, so sums of
three of them realize every integer in [-3,3] -- that is 7 consecutive values,
hence ALL of Z/7.  (Contrast mod 9: [-3,3] is only 7 of the 9 classes, and the
two missed classes are exactly +-4.)  Same {0,+-1} cube image, opposite verdict:
the modulus size decides.  Mod 7 imposes nothing.

==============================================================================
PART 2 -- THE 2026 OPEN LEDGER FOR x^3+y^3+z^3 = k, k < 1000  [WEB-VERIFIED]
==============================================================================
OPEN (no representation known), k < 1000: [114, 390, 627, 633, 732, 921, 975]
smallest open k = 114
Source (accessed 2026-06-10): Wikipedia 'Sums of three cubes', verbatim:
  'The only remaining unsolved cases up to 1,000 are the seven numbers
   114, 390, 627, 633, 732, 921, and 975, and there are no known primitive
   solutions (i.e. gcd(x,y,z)=1) for 192, 375, and 600.'
NOTE: 579 is NOT open -- it fell in September 2019 (Booker-Sutherland, same
Charity Engine run as 42; Wikipedia verbatim: '...as well as solutions for
several other previously unknown cases including n=165 and 579 for n<=1000.')
The human dispatch's candidate list included 579: corrected here.

mod-9 audit of the open list (and the famous fallen cases):
  k =  114: k mod 9 = 6  [-3 (==6)]
  k =  390: k mod 9 = 3  [+3]
  k =  627: k mod 9 = 6  [-3 (==6)]
  k =  633: k mod 9 = 3  [+3]
  k =  732: k mod 9 = 3  [+3]
  k =  921: k mod 9 = 3  [+3]
  k =  975: k mod 9 = 3  [+3]
  [PASS] every open k < 1000 is == +-3 (mod 9): residual = 0
  fallen k =    3: k mod 9 = 3
  fallen k =   33: k mod 9 = 6
  fallen k =   42: k mod 9 = 6
  fallen k =  165: k mod 9 = 3
  fallen k =  579: k mod 9 = 3
  fallen k =  906: k mod 9 = 6
VERIFIED(list of 7): all seven open values are == +-3 (mod 9) -- exactly the
rigid class of PART 3b.  The famous fallen cases 3, 33, 42, 165, 579, 906 were
also all == +-3 (mod 9).  This is a structural observation about a finite list,
NOT a law about which k are hard (MISTAKE-028/036/055 discipline).

==============================================================================
HEATH-BROWN COMPLETENESS -- status: CONJECTURE
==============================================================================
CONJECTURE (Heath-Brown 1992, 'The density of zeros of forms for which weak
approximation fails', Math. Comp. 59):  every k != +-4 (mod 9) has a
representation x^3+y^3+z^3 = k, and in fact infinitely many.
Status 2026: open.  No representation is known for k = 114; no algorithm is
even known to decide representability for a single given k.
Mod 9 is the only known congruence obstruction: the form x^3+y^3+z^3 - k has
zeros in every Z_p (p != 3) and in Z_3 iff k != +-4 (mod 9); failure for
k == +-4 (mod 9) is a pure 3-adic (mod 9) phenomenon, cf. PART 3a.

